    <property name="geometry">
     <rect>
      <x>71</x>
      <y>57</y>
      <width>416</width>
      <height>26</height>
     </rect>
    </property>
    <property name="toolTip">
     <string>The folder mbmesh writes mesh.glb and the other outputs to; created when missing. Empty = beside the input, named after it (&lt;name&gt;_mbmesh). The points of a LAS or x,y,z input are also written there, as mbmesh reads them (mbmesh_points.xyt and its datalist mbmesh_input.mb-1).</string>
    </property>
   </widget>
   <widget class="QLabel" name="lbl_srs">
    <property name="geometry">
     <rect>
      <x>11</x>
      <y>87</y>
      <width>54</width>
      <height>26</height>
     </rect>
    </property>
    <property name="text">
     <string>CRS</string>
    </property>
   </widget>
   <widget class="QLineEdit" name="p_srs">
    <property name="geometry">
     <rect>
      <x>71</x>
      <y>87</y>
      <width>416</width>
      <height>26</height>
     </rect>
    </property>
    <property name="toolTip">
     <string>The coordinate system of the points when the file does not say it and they are not longitude and latitude: an EPSG code (EPSG:3763) or a PROJ string. LAS/LAZ files are read without their coordinate system, so a projected LAS file needs it here. Empty = the file's own, or longitude and latitude. Not used for MB-System data, which is always in longitude and latitude.</string>
    </property>
    <property name="placeholderText">
     <string>the file's own</string>
    </property>
   </widget>
  </widget>
